{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And I will set redemption between My people and your people.</b> He already mentioned that He would make a distinction between the land of Goshen and the land of Egypt, but this redemption is that even in the land of Egypt, if the beasts find any Jew there, they will do him no harm and no destruction, and they will eat the Egyptian people. And so David said (Psalms 78:45): ״ישלח בהם ערוב ויאכלם״, and this is the sense of פדות, in the manner of what is written (Isaiah 43:3): ״נתתי כפרך מצרים״. And you will find the word פדות spelled defective, without a ו״ו, because the redemption of Egypt is a redemption after which there is subjugation; but the future redemption has no subjugation after it, only everlasting deliverance, and therefore you will find in the future redemption פדות written full, with a ו״ו — as it is written (Psalms 111:9): ״פדות שלח לעמו״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:05.688626769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}